This project builds on research by Always Foundation (https://github.com/alwaysfoundation):
- The Creed propositions and excluded errors in src/dust/data/creed.json are adapted and
  extended from ai/creed/nicene-381.json in alwaysfoundation/always-platform,
  "Always Foundation, CC BY 4.0" (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  Changes: split into 24 atomic propositions with logical literals, Greek anchors and
  Scripture references; excluded errors extended from 5 to 16; latitude topics added.
- src/dust/data/constitution.md is adapted in part from the Always AI assistant
  instructions (Always Foundation, CC BY 4.0).
- docs/theology.md, docs/methods.md, docs/privacy.md and docs/model-family.md draw on
  Always Foundation's position paper "Christian AI Alignment and the Nicene Creed of 381",
  its Always AI research paper and ADRs 0015-0018 (CC BY 4.0), with changes.
The Always name and logo are trademarks of Always Foundation and are not used to brand Dust.

Texts:
- The Nicene Creed, English: traditional translation in the public domain (onthewing.org via
  NonlinearFruit/Creeds.json), as used by Always Foundation.
- The Creed in Greek (381, as read at Chalcedon 451) and Latin (Roman Rite): public domain.
- Scripture in src/dust/data/scripture.json: World English Bible, public domain.

Model weights: src/dust/data/guard-v0.npz is a small classifier trained only on the
synthetic data in data/train.jsonl, released under Apache-2.0. No third-party model
weights are included.
